# Docker env file with generated secrets (template lives in .env.docker.example)
.env.docker
# The LOCAL docker env file holds the same generated secrets (JWT_SECRET,
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD, ...). It was staged for commit once, which is exactly the
# mistake this line prevents: `.env.docker` was covered but `.env.docker.local`
# was not, and the file's own comment says "generated secrets".
.env.docker.local
